@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "About this deployment";
}

<div class="row justify-content-center">
    <div class="col-md-8">
        <h1 class="h4 mb-3">About this deployment</h1>

        <p>
            StudyMate is a portfolio project. This deployment exists to demonstrate how the
            matching works, not to run a real study-partner service.
        </p>

        <h2 class="h6 text-uppercase text-muted mt-4">The students are not real</h2>
        <p>
            Every profile you see is fictional and generated from a fixed script. Names,
            courses, availability and biographies are invented. Any resemblance to a real
            person is accidental.
        </p>

        <h2 class="h6 text-uppercase text-muted mt-4">If you create an account</h2>
        <p>
            Registration works, and your password is hashed rather than stored as text. But
            the hosting tier this runs on has no persistent storage: the database is rebuilt
            from scratch whenever the service restarts, redeploys, or spins down after about
            fifteen minutes without traffic.
        </p>
        <p>
            Anything you enter — your account, your profile, requests you send — is therefore
            temporary and will disappear without warning. Please do not enter information you
            would mind losing, and do not reuse a password from anywhere else.
        </p>

        <h2 class="h6 text-uppercase text-muted mt-4">What is not here</h2>
        <p>
            There is no email verification, no password reset, no moderation tooling and no
            way to report another user. Those would all be prerequisites for running this as
            a real service, and they are deliberately out of scope.
        </p>

        <h2 class="h6 text-uppercase text-muted mt-4">Tracking</h2>
        <p>
            No analytics, no advertising and no third-party trackers. The only cookie is the
            one that keeps you signed in.
        </p>

        <p class="mt-4">
            <a asp-controller="Home" asp-action="Index">Back to the start</a>
        </p>
    </div>
</div>
